<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <meta name="description" content="Demonstration of different CSS selector types.">
    <meta name="author" content="Pranav Arora">
    <title>CSS Selector Types - Pranav Arora</title>
    <style>
        /* 1. Universal Selector */
        * {
            box-sizing: border-box;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
        }
        /* 2. Element Selector */
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background: #eef2f7;
            color: #222;
            padding: 2rem;
            line-height: 1.6;
        }
        h1 {
            margin-bottom: 1rem;
            color: #1d3557;
        }
        p {
            margin-bottom: .75rem;
        }
        /* 3. Class Selector */
        .card {
            background: #fff;
            padding: 1rem;
            margin-bottom: 1rem;
            border-radius: 8px;
            box-shadow: 0 1px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, .15);
        }
        .highlight {
            background: #ffe066;
            padding: 0 .25rem;
        }
        /* 4. ID Selector */
        #special {
            border-left: 6px solid #e63946;
        }
        /* 5. Grouping Selector */
        h2, h3 {
            color: #457b9d;
            margin-bottom: .5rem;
        }
        /* 6. Descendant Selector */
        .card a {
            color: #e63946;
        }
        /* 7. Child Selector */
        ul > li {
            margin-left: 1.5rem;
        }
        /* 8. Adjacent Sibling Selector */
        h2 + p {
            font-weight: bold;
        }
        /* 9. Attribute Selector */
        a[target="_blank"]::after {
            content: " ↗";
        }
        input[type="text"] {
            padding: .4rem;
            border: 1px solid #999;
            border-radius: 4px;
        }
        /* 10. Pseudo-classes */
        a:hover {
            text-decoration: none;
            background: #ffe066;
        }
        input:focus {
            outline: 3px solid #a8dadc;
        }
        li:nth-child(odd) {
            color: #1d3557;
        }
        /* 11. Pseudo-element */
        p::first-line {
            letter-spacing: .5px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>CSS Selector Playground</h1>
    <p>Created by Pranav Arora | BCA Artificial Intelligence</p>
    <p>Invertis University</p>
    <div class="card">
        <h2>Class and Element Selectors</h2>
        <p>
            This paragraph demonstrates the
            <span class="highlight">highlight class selector</span>.
        </p>
        <p>This is a normal paragraph styled by the element selector.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card" id="special">
        <h3>ID Selector</h3>
        <p>
            This card uses a unique ID selector
            to create a red left border.
        </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
        <h3>Descendant, Child and Pseudo-class Selectors</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Odd item using nth-child</li>
            <li>Even item</li>
            <li>
                Odd item with
                <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/"
                   target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                    MDN Website
                </a>
            </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            <input type="text" placeholder="Click here to test focus">
        </p>
    </div>
    <footer>
        <p>&copy; 2026 Pranav Arora | Invertis University</p>
    </footer>
</body>
</html>
